includes: First feature of the all-in-one production pivot — the linear SONG ARRANGEMENT. Tools → Arrangement opens a timeline editor: chain sections, point each at a captured Session clip, set its bar length (scrub field), reorder / rename / delete, and Play the whole song with loop — the playhead highlights the sounding section. It rides the one shared transport (no second clock): on each bar boundary the song advances and loads the next section's clip BEFORE that bar's notes trigger, so sections change cleanly. Built on the existing tested Arrangement/ArrangementStore/ArrangementPlayer domain (was unwired); Session clips were already live (Tools → Clips). No new dependencies. (Next pivot waves: video capture/edit, RTMP broadcast, Ableton Link — separate gated cycles.) Verified: ci.yml (build+test, all platforms) + xcode-compile-check (AUv3) green on 3d56b23. Plus everything from v10.34.3–v10.34.12.
